# Source file length and post-change refactor

## Scope

Applies to `.rb` files in the repo root and `lib/`. Skip generated outputs and vendored trees.

## Line-count target

Keep source files at **200 lines or fewer**. If a feature cannot fit without harm, split into the smallest reasonable modules and note why briefly.

## Trigger

Applies to any **modified** file when **either**:

- it **was** ≥200 lines before your edit, **or**
- it **became** ≥200 lines after your edit.

When triggered, you **must** extract or DRY **at least 100 lines** from that file before you stop (or until it is ≤200 lines if that requires fewer).

"No time", "unrelated to my fix", and "it was already long" do **not** exempt a file you modified.

## After each edit

When you finish a coherent change (one task or one PR-worth of edits):

1. Among **files you modified**, find every file that matches the **Trigger** above.
2. For each triggered file, shrink it before you stop:
   - **Prefer extraction**: move **≥100 lines** of self-contained logic into another module, **or**
   - **Prefer cleanup when enough**: remove duplicate logic (DRY) and dead code until the file drops by **≥100 lines** or reaches **≤200 lines** — whichever comes first.
3. If several files trigger, start with the **longest**; do **not** refactor other long files you did not touch unless asked.

## How to shrink (pick one or combine)

| Approach | When to use |
|----------|-------------|
| **Extract to a module** | Cohesive unit (class, module, method group) that belongs elsewhere |
| **DRY cleanup** | Duplicated logic can merge into shared helpers without changing behaviour |
| **Dead-code removal** | Unused methods, params, constants, or branches confirmed unreferenced |

## Extraction rules

- Move only self-contained units — **no unrelated rewrites**.
- Respect **SOLID**: each extracted module has one clear responsibility.
- **Preserve all existing behaviour** exactly — structural change only.
- Prefer **one** new module over many tiny files; use Zeitwerk autoloading via `lib/loader`.
- Match project naming (`snake_case` files, `PascalCase` modules) and `require_relative` patterns used nearby.
- Use dependency injection when the extracted module needs collaborators.
